<!--T:2-->
{{GuiCommand
|Name=Std SendToPythonConsole
|MenuLocation=Edit → Send to Python Console
|Workbenches=All
|Shortcut={{KEY|Ctrl}}+{{KEY|Shift}}+{{KEY|P}}
|Version=0.19
}}

==Description== <!--T:3-->

<!--T:4-->
The '''Std SendToPythonConsole''' command creates variables in the [[Python_Console|Python Console]] referencing selected objects and selected subobjects, along with some other useful variables. They can be used in the development of Python code.

<!--T:14-->
The following variables are created:

<!--T:15-->
{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Variable name !! Referenced object(s)
|-
| {{Incode|sels}} || A list of selection objects (one for each selected object)
|-
| {{Incode|sel}} || The last item in {{Incode|sels}} (belonging to the last selected object)
|-
| {{Incode|doc}} || The document containing the selected objects
|-
| {{Incode|objs}} || A list with an item for each selected object:<br>
The selected object itself (if it is not a Link)<br>
The linked object (if the selected object is a Link)
|-
| {{Incode|obj}} || The last item in {{Incode|objs}} (belonging to the last selected object)
|-
| {{Incode|lnks}} || A list with an item for each selected object:<br>
The selected object itself (if it is a Link)<br>
{{Incode|None}} (if the selected object is not a Link)
|-
| {{Incode|lnk}} || The last item in {{Incode|lnks}} (belonging to the last selected object)
|-
| {{Incode|shps}} || A list with an item for each {{Incode|obj}} in {{Incode|objs}}:<br>
The {{Incode|Shape}} property of {{Incode|obj}} for objects that have that property<br>
The {{Incode|Mesh}} property of {{Incode|obj}} for Mesh objects<br>
The {{Incode|Points}} property of {{Incode|obj}} for Points objects<br>
{{None}} for other objects
|-
| {{Incode|shp}} || The last item in {{Incode|shps}} (belonging to the last item in {{Incode|objs}})
|-
| {{Incode|subs}} || A list with the selected subobjects. The list is empty if no subobjects have been selected.
|-
| {{Incode|sub}} || The last item in {{Incode|subs}}, or {{Incode|None}} if {{Incode|subs}} is empty.
|-
| {{Incode|names}} || A list with a tuple for each selected object. Each tuple contains the names of the subobjects belonging to that object. The tuple is empty if no subobjects have been selected for the object.
|-
| {{Incode|name}} || The last item in the last tuple in {{Incode|names}}, or {{Incode|None}} if that tuple is empty.
|}

==Usage== <!--T:5-->

<!--T:13-->
# Select one or more objects and/or one or more subobjects belonging to one or more objects.
# There are several ways to invoke the command:
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Edit → [[Image:Std_SendToPythonConsole.svg|16px]] Send to Python Console}} option from the menu.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|[[Image:Std_SendToPythonConsole.svg|16px]] Send to Python Console}} option from the [[Tree_View|Tree View]] context menu or [[3D_View|3D View]] context menu.
#* Use the keyboard shortcut: {{KEY|Ctrl}}+{{KEY|Shift}}+{{KEY|P}}.
# If required the [[Python_Console|Python Console]] opens.
# The [[Python_Console|Python Console]] receives the keyboard focus.

==Notes== <!--T:16-->

<!--T:17-->
* All previously created variables are deleted each time the command is run.

<!--T:18-->
* For selected objects that are Links ({{Incode|App::Link}}) and whose linked object has a {{Incode|Shape}}, the item in {{Incode|shps}} will be the shape of the linked object. If the Links have been transformed or scaled and you want to access the scaled/transformed shapes, you can do so with this code:

</translate>
: {{Code|code=
lnk_shps = [Part.getShape(l) if l else None for l in lnks]
lnk_shp = Part.getShape(lnk) if lnk else None
}}
